      "description": "UCONN - Jobs UCONN Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. Oops! Please check your email for errors! Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Closes Sep 25 2026 Pre-Award Specialist - Faculty Shared Services in UConn Storrs The Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) is recruiting talented grants and contracts/sponsored project professionals to join our research administration team. The Pre-Award Grants and Contracts Specialists provide day to day management and oversight for a high volume of pre-award administration. Closes Sep 25 2026 Director of Research Technology Services in UConn Storrs Under the general direction of the Chief Information Officer, provides executive, technical, and operational leadership for technology services supporting the University’s research enterprise within Information Technology Services (ITS). The Director is responsible for developing and implementing solutions, policies, and services that advance the University’s research mission through effective use of technology. The Director serves as the primary liaison between ITS, the Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR), faculty researchers, research centers, and other stakeholders to ensure that technology services effectively support current and emerging research needs and has a dotted line reporting relationship to the Vice President for Research, Innovation and Entrepreneurship. Closes Sep 18 2026 IT Manager in UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut Information Technology Services (ITS) is seeking a Manager of Network Engineering and Operations to lead the University's Network Engineering and Network Operations teams. This position is responsible for overseeing the daily operation, support, and continuous improvement of the University's enterprise network infrastructure and services that support the academic, research, administrative, and residential communities across the Storrs campus, regional campuses, and the School of Law. Closes Sep 17 2026 Student Employment Manager in UConn Storrs UConn Recreation is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented professional to serve as our Student Employment Manager.  In this impactful role, the manager will help support the student employee experience by coordinating key human resources functions, including recruitment, onboarding, and payroll administration. Closes Sep 24 2026 Cash Operations Specialist in UConn Storrs The Cash Operations Specialist serves as the primary financial administrator in the Office of the Bursar for University deposits, responsible for daily reconciliation of incoming funds between the University’s bank accounts and the State and University general ledger systems. This position monitors departments’ compliance with State statutes for depositing and provides training assistance to University staff for depositing and cash handling. More Jobs 73 Powered by PageUp Full site © 2026 UCONN"
